{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires","id":1411761,"title":"Gods and Vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-04T01:56:12-07:00","id":1411761,"title":"Gods and Vampires?","content":"In VtM some gods are vampires actually (Mithras, Set, Osiris, etc.), some \u201cgods\u201d are faked by vampires (Shaitan, etc.). I wonder if there\u2019s a list or thread discusses this? Or do you know more guys like this?<br /> <br /> And: I wonder if the Odin hated by Get of Fenris is the same guy in Wolves of Sea, a Gangrel? I think it\u2019s not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T03:17:46-07:00","id":1411766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires#post1411761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In VtM some gods are vampires actually (Mithras, Set, Osiris, etc.), some \u201cgods\u201d are faked by vampires (Shaitan, etc.). I wonder if there\u2019s a list or thread discusses this? Or do you know more guys like this?<br /> <br /> And: I wonder if the Odin hated by Get of Fenris is the same guy in Wolves of Sea, a Gangrel? I think it\u2019s not</div> </div> </div> </div>My view on the subject is that some vampires view themselves as gods but all vampires who are gods are just vampires impersonating deities. The gods of the Earth are mysterious and powerful beings that can empower human faith but Kindred cults are just that, cults.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I do state that Mithras may very well have been a demigod that was the honest-to-God son of a god before being Embraced but he's still &quot;just&quot; a vampire.<br /> <br /> They're no more gods than the Gould from Stargate SG-1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T05:01:16-07:00","id":1411773,"title":"","content":"god isn't a splat or a race, it's a title,<br /> anything, including a mere mortal can be a god<br /> <br /> now, what splat is each god? who came first? who impersonated who? is unclear (cause white wolf)<br /> <br /> shaitan is a known impersonator, that doesn't make him any less of a god","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-04-2020, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T06:30:45-07:00","id":1411778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires#post1411761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In VtM some gods are vampires actually (Mithras, Set, Osiris, etc.), some \u201cgods\u201d are faked by vampires (Shaitan, etc.). I wonder if there\u2019s a list or thread discusses this? Or do you know more guys like this?<br /> <br /> And: I wonder if the Odin hated by Get of Fenris is the same guy in Wolves of Sea, a Gangrel? I think it\u2019s not</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple vampires are said to have taken the semblance of Odin and other gods and the Allfather is a charlatan that diablerized his way up to 5th gen.<br /> <br /> The Vargr of the Norse lands recall their history descending from Cainarl who was made into a vampire by Odin, thus indicating the original Odin wasn't a vampire, or that Cainarl wasn't the first vampire and the gods were for some reason.<br /> <br /> Fenrir recall two separate beings with the mantle of Wotan, one in the super ancient past and a reincarnation in the more reasonable past.<br /> <br /> We also know two ancient Vampires fought for territory in ancient Ireland either imitating or inspiring the Dagda and the Morrigan.<br /> <br /> Then we have Samedi...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And a vampire who imitated Mictlan.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T08:33:23-07:00","id":1411802,"title":"","content":"My take is the vampires are usually faking it - they usually rip off the name of a god and some of the vampires manage to get away with this for ages. Such as Mithras. There probably was (and might still be) a Celestine Mithras, or the actual god. Mithras the vampire just took the name of the god, and eventually thought he was a god. But they are not the same creature. The same goes for Odin.<br /> <br /> Set is possibly a different case, as the vampire at least was an utter liar but it is difficult to tell at this remove.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T08:54:58-07:00","id":1411804,"title":"","content":"I also tend to think that humans worship or venerated a god and then the vampires comes in to try and take advantage of it.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that corruption is almost inherent to vampires, them being more powerful and having advantages over humans, and so it follows known courses that they would corrupt and use things that normal people hold dear to the vampires' advantage<br /> <br /> The name &quot;Baali&quot; used by those specific vampires seem like an utter perversion when looking at the character of Baal in the Baal Cycle.<br /> <br /> EDITED: Fixed some weird English","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:10:10-07:00","id":1411809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411802#post1411802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take is the vampires are usually faking it - they usually rip off the name of a god and some of the vampires manage to get away with this for ages. Such as Mithras. There probably was (and might still be) a Celestine Mithras, or the actual god. Mithras the vampire just took the name of the god, and eventually thought he was a god. But they are not the same creature. The same goes for Odin.<br /> <br /> Set is possibly a different case, as the vampire at least was an utter liar but it is difficult to tell at this remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to point out the Pooka claim and have treasures that back up that the Egyptian Gods were all Pooka thus the whole &quot;animal head&quot; thing. What we think of as Set or Mithras is a mix of things that have been brought together by a culture. Mithras the vampire.. did ride the cult of Mithras but the Cult of Mithras seems to be have been &quot;made up&quot; almost whole heartedly by romans around the turn o the C.E. and have no connection with Mithras the Sun God of Persia.<br /> <br /> Given we know that IRL it wouldn't be too much of a a stretch to argue The Cult of Mithras may have been constructed in part MIthras the Vampire. On the other hand there are still Celestial Chorus members who follow the Cult as was laid out in ancient times and is lost irl who see it as a path to the One. These are not necissarily a choice of Either OR here. They Mithras the vampire may have tried to manipulate something he couldn't quite control.<br /> <br /> Odin is probably equally complicated as the Odin we have now is not the Odin worshiped by the vikings but the records by Christians who had long since been converted. What was the living oral tradition probably contained aspect of potenially multiple things.. Fairy Lords, Vampires, Celestial entities.. that you could meet 3 or more Odins in a bar and each being True makes things complicated.<br /> <br /> Ultimately Religion changes over time. And Vampires are master manipulators or at least that's what they claim. So hollowing out a Faith an putting yourself up there wouldn't be unheard of...but its hard to tell what &quot;came first&quot; and if that even matters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:28:31-07:00","id":1411814,"title":"","content":"To be honest I think vampires always fake gods. Spirits of named gods (most are Incarna level I think) will crush down those vampires utterly. Think about spirit \u201cMithras\u201d, \u201cSet\u201d or even \u201cShiva\u201d...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T09:46:15-07:00","id":1411816,"title":"","content":"Mmmmh yes and no. Very powerful Meths tend to be also powerful blood mages, and blood magic can do astonishing things to spirits. Odin was capable of putting the muzzle on Great Fenris, Set banished the Silent Striders from their lands, and Baba Yaga was capable of summoning one of the Wyrm Talons into existence, Menele's magic awoke an immense spirit of fire that destroyed Pompei and so on.<br /> Even vampires like Mithras, who lack blood magic, surrounds themselves with &quot;high priests&quot; like Cretheus, who had Thauma 8, and Cretheus was capable of binding spirits and demons to his will.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:05:59-07:00","id":1411819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411816#post1411816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmmh yes and no. Very powerful Meths tend to be also powerful blood mages, and blood magic can do astonishing things to spirits. Odin was capable of putting the muzzle on Great Fenris, Set banished the Silent Striders from their lands, and Baba Yaga was capable of summoning one of the Wyrm Talons into existence, Menele's magic awoke an immense spirit of fire that destroyed Pompei and so on.<br /> Even vampires like Mithras, who lack blood magic, surrounds themselves with &quot;high priests&quot; like Cretheus, who had Thauma 8, and Cretheus was capable of binding spirits and demons to his will.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry but we don\u2019t know if the Odin in Fenris legend is the same vampiric guy. And to be honest I think Baba Yaga is confused, <br /> <br /> A World of Rage says she is greater than a Maeljin Incarna (aka. A 4th gens like her can crush a Maeljin... the greatest servant of Wyrm)<br /> She bound Talon of Wyrm when she was a SORCERER<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Set did banish Striders, but just that. Setites did much more horrible thing to Bubasti, another kind of Fera. They slaughtered all cat kin but ghouled and imprisoned several... if they knew animal kin was the core of a shapeshifter tribe then the Bubasti would decease long long ago... thank you, Shu-Horus, the greatest Striders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:14:57-07:00","id":1411822,"title":"","content":"what's the problem with Baba Yaga being greater than an Incarna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:20:21-07:00","id":1411824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411814#post1411814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I think vampires always fake gods. Spirits of named gods (most are Incarna level I think) will crush down those vampires utterly. Think about spirit \u201cMithras\u201d, \u201cSet\u201d or even \u201cShiva\u201d...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, in Mage at least, Spirits aren't actually appearing as gods usually. If you're an Order of Hermes mage and go to meet an Incarnae of Jupiter then you may see the Archangel Michael, Zeus, Odin, or other patriarchal male authority figure.<br /> <br /> And they will act the part because your unconscious is filling in a lot of &quot;What Man Was Not Meant To Know.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411822#post1411822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what's the problem with Baba Yaga being greater than an Incarna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can control gods and spirits with true names. It's an annoyance to demons and gods both.<br /> <br /> Magic is the ultimate cheat codes of the universe.<br /> <br /> Blame the fact that avatars are fragments of the Pure Ones and One, which is the Spirit of Everything (God? Perhaps--or maybe just the closest to it in the setting)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:24:42-07:00","id":1411826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411822#post1411822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what's the problem with Baba Yaga being greater than an Incarna?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even more, this is stated by a Werewolf Sourcebook, not by a vampire sourcebook.<br /> The war against Baba Yaga was big stuff in Werewolf, one of the biggest metaplot thing in the line. It was the most important thing happened to Europe's werewolves, and the stepping stone Margrave Konietzko used to challenge the Silver Fangs dominance in the Garou Nation. The great alliance between Get of Fenris, Black Furies and Shadow Lords that is reshaping eastern europe was made to create a front against the Hag.<br /> <br /> So yeah, by the werewolf's metaplot (and, note, not by Vampire's metaplot) Baba Yaga has been bigger stuff than the Maeljin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-04-2020, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:30:55-07:00","id":1411828,"title":"","content":"This is a really awesome discussion. I think all you guys make some good points. And I\u2019m not entirely convinced Baba Yaga is really dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:14:54-07:00","id":1411851,"title":"","content":"Vampires are not gods in any sense of the word. They sometimes manage to create cults that revere them as such but more often hijack existing cults portraying themselves as gods for a subsect of mortals. That is actually the case with Mithras. Check out DA Mage: Grimoire for confirmation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:22:00-07:00","id":1411852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411822#post1411822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what's the problem with Baba Yaga being greater than an Incarna?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even a 4th generation Vampire as experienced as Baba Yaga doesn't work on the same palying filed of the Incarnae and Celestines. Vampires by becoming vampires are bascially creatures of the tellurian and as far as the Umbrae go they can visit the shadowlands with a modicum of difficulty (it requires dedicated discipline), Incarnae work on a different scale, that's to say Baba Yaga's personal power can certainly be a match for an Incarna (not the most powerful of them maybe) but the Incarna doesn't need to face Baba Yaga directly to win.<br /> That said Baba Yaga is a bad example for this because she had several armies of mystical servants including mages and even a demon so she could very well have had the firepower required to face Incarnae by proxy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:39:47-07:00","id":1411855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411819#post1411819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but we don\u2019t know if the Odin in Fenris legend is the same vampiric guy. And to be honest I think Baba Yaga is confused,<br /> <br /> A World of Rage says she is greater than a Maeljin Incarna (aka. A 4th gens like her can crush a Maeljin... the greatest servant of Wyrm)<br /> She bound Talon of Wyrm when she was a SORCERER<br /> ...<br /> <br /> Set did banish Striders, but just that. Setites did much more horrible thing to Bubasti, another kind of Fera. They slaughtered all cat kin but ghouled and imprisoned several... if they knew animal kin was the core of a shapeshifter tribe then the Bubasti would decease long long ago... thank you, Shu-Horus, the greatest Striders</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol the same talon of the Wyrm that fought Absimilliard and made him flee? A World of Rage says the Baba Yaga was &quot;a truly ancient being with power nearing that of a Maeljin Incarna, she was a creature of the Wyld, corrupt true, but with her own vision for Russia's future&quot;.<br /> <br /> So no, even in aWoR Baba Yaga is presented as ALMOST as powerful as a Maeljin Incarna, not as more powerful than one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:44:00-07:00","id":1411856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411852#post1411852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even a 4th generation Vampire as experienced as Baba Yaga doesn't work on the same palying filed of the Incarnae and Celestines. Vampires by becoming vampires are bascially creatures of the tellurian and as far as the Umbrae go they can visit the shadowlands with a modicum of difficulty (it requires dedicated discipline), Incarnae work on a different scale, that's to say Baba Yaga's personal power can certainly be a match for an Incarna (not the most powerful of them maybe) but the Incarna doesn't need to face Baba Yaga directly to win.<br /> That said Baba Yaga is a bad example for this because she had several armies of mystical servants including mages and even a demon so she could very well have had the firepower required to face Incarnae by proxy.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks, but that's not what I'm asking,<br /> <br /> I'm asking what's the issue with baba yaga being greater than an Incarnae,<br /> whether she is indeed greater or not doesn't matter to me,<br /> Rock113 just seems opposed to the idea of her being a god, and (if that's truly the case) I'm curious to know why he is opposed to the idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-04-2020, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:48:30-07:00","id":1411859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411856#post1411856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thanks, but that's not what I'm asking,<br /> <br /> I'm asking what's the issue with baba yaga being greater than an Incarnae,<br /> whether she is indeed greater or not doesn't matter to me,<br /> Rock113 just seems opposed to the idea of her being a god, and I'm curious to know why he is opposed to the idea</div> </div> </div> </div>She is not a god in any sense of the word. Gods in the WoD are spirits and Vampires are spiritually stunted cursed beings. Baba Yaga is a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:58:58-07:00","id":1411862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411856#post1411856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm asking what's the issue with baba yaga being greater than an Incarnae,</div> </div> </div> </div>She should not have had the power to subdue a god, even at her age and relative power. The god should have been out of her reach. But the writers needed her to be the Big Bad of the campaign and book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:11:37-07:00","id":1411864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411859#post1411859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She is not a god in any sense of the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>God, noun. A superhuman being or spirit, worshipped as having power over nature or human fortunes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIs she superhuman? Yes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIs she a being or spirit? Yes.<br /> <br /> \u200bIs she worshipped? I honestly don't know. But if she is, well, that's the barrier for entry.<br /> <br /> The Incredible Hulk would be just as divine as Thor if he had a religion venerating him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baba Yaga is a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that doesn't mean she can't be a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:33:16-07:00","id":1411869,"title":"","content":"Menele can destroy entire cities in blaze of fire and make volcanoes erupt; he is faster than any being on earth; he can use cars in the same way I use baseball bats, he can reshape any memories and possess any beings, just by touching them; he can become invisible and make people kneel just with his presence; his skin is harder than steel; he can read minds, project his spirit anywhere in the world; he can shift in any kind of animal, or just become wind; he is far more intelligent than most spirits, and he can control any spirits he wish thanks to his magic,or set thing aflame with a snap of finger, and make your blood boil like a cauldron...<br /> <br /> Why Menele isn't a god?<br /> <br /> <br /> If we must use the judaic meaning of god than nothing is a god, not even Incarnas (and not even Celestines for sure).<br /> <br /> Spirit Incarna are not omnipowerful, nor omnipotent or omnipresent and for sure they are not eternal (some Incarna are younger than many Methuselah).<br /> Not even the Triat would fit the judaic prerequisite of godhood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's take a look at the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> They are not eternal<br /> The Duke of Steel is just 500 years old, Aliara is 1200 years old, Aife is 600 years old, Hellbringer is at most 1400 years old, and Kernel, Choke, Collum and Yul are probably no older than 1000 years. Which means that Baba Yaga is...14-7 times older than many Maeljin Incarna.<br /> <br /> <br /> They are not creators of the universe (as every Incarna is created by a Celestine)<br /> <br /> They are not omnipresent (Maeljin Incarna especially, since they are confinated to the Duchies of Malfeas).<br /> <br /> They are not immortal, as any of them can be killed, and some have been.<br /> <br /> <br /> They are not omnipowerful: Aliara's charms can be resisted, you can lie to her and you can betray her; The Duke of Steel can be captured and imprisoned, and he has no powers once you take his mask; Aife can be killed by ANY pattern spider, or by any creature that is indifferent to pain; Hellbringer can be tricked into killing himself, and MAliq Harjaq can be poisoned and killed; Knight Entropy can be killed by exposure to the Flux Realm; Maine duBois can fail the task you give him with a contract; Doge Klypse can be made mortal again if you find the box with his mortal memories; Nameless Angel can be killed with a powerful ritual;<br /> <br /> And so on...nothing of these could be done to &quot;a god&quot;. You cannot kidnapp God, or trick him into signing a contract he can't fulfill.<br /> <br /> From wikipedia<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><b>Conceptions of God</b> in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monotheism\" target=\"_blank\">monotheist</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantheism\" target=\"_blank\">pantheist</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panentheism\" target=\"_blank\">panentheist</a> religions \u2013 or of the supreme deity in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henotheistic\" target=\"_blank\">henotheistic</a> religions \u2013 can extend to various levels of abstraction:</span></span><ul><li>as a powerful, human-like, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">supernatural</a> being, or as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apotheosis\" target=\"_blank\">deification</a> of an <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Esotericism\" target=\"_blank\">esoteric</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystical\" target=\"_blank\">mystical</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophical\" target=\"_blank\">philosophical</a> entity or category;</li> <li>as the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ultimate_(philosophy)\" target=\"_blank\">Ultimate</a>&quot;, the <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summum_bonum\" target=\"_blank\">summum bonum</a></i>, the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absolute_Infinite\" target=\"_blank\">Absolute Infinite</a>&quot;, the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transcendence_(religion)\" target=\"_blank\">Transcendent</a>&quot;, or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existence\" target=\"_blank\">Existence</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Being\" target=\"_blank\">Being</a> itself;</li> <li>as the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ground_of_being\" target=\"_blank\">ground of being</a>, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monism\" target=\"_blank\">monistic</a> <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/substrate\" target=\"_blank\">substrate</a>, that which we cannot understand; and so on.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">The first recordings that survive of monotheistic conceptions of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/God\" target=\"_blank\">God</a>, borne out of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henotheism\" target=\"_blank\">henotheism</a> and (mostly in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_religions\" target=\"_blank\">Eastern religions</a>) <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monism\" target=\"_blank\">monism</a>, are from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellenistic_period\" target=\"_blank\">Hellenistic period</a><b>. Of the many objects and entities that religions and other belief systems across the ages have labeled as divine, the one criterion they share is their acknowledgment as divine by a group or groups of human beings.</b></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-04-2020, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T14:32:12-07:00","id":1411885,"title":"","content":"Yet in the context of the World of Darkness a god is a very specific kind of being and Baba Yaga or any other vampire is not a god. They can very well impersonate one, their followers may even have faith in them... but they are still not gods in the WoD sense of the word as they don't even have a way to channel the spiritual energy generated by faith (unlike creatures like Earthbound demons, that are still not gods but are at least more spiritually &quot;advanced&quot; than vampires).<br /> <br /> In the context of the WoD a god is a spirit, usually a powerful one. Age is a less important factor for their power than it is for vampires because as spiritual beings gods have different ways to generate and accumulate power compared to vampires who havew to learn to exploit the curse placed on their blood (curses plural, actually).<br /> <br /> And again, in the context of the WoD a vampire is a cursed being. The curse(s) gives the vampire power but also stunt their spiritual growth limiting them to the tellurian with the sole exception of the shadowlands for a few of them.<br /> <br /> Now it's all well and good that the judeo/christian definition of God (note the capital G) does not conform to anything existing in the WoD (possibly not even the creator of the angels/demons), but that's simply stating the obvious because that definition implies an omniscent and omnipotent being who is the sum of everything that exists (I'm obviously simplyfing things here, the definition of what God was supposed to be was debated a lot in theology and is still debated today). Basically it has nothing to do with the world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 09-04-2020, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T14:34:41-07:00","id":1411887,"title":"","content":"Spirits are Spirits, they are not gods by definition. Even more by Werewolf lore the only things that can be compared to gods are Celestines, not Incarna.<br /> And in the context of the Wod as a whole that's even more true, because we could use mage's definitions of goodhood, and we know pretty well that umbroods are not gods (and even here only Celestines are considered akin to &quot;gods&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> Book of Madness<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DIVINITY<br /> I hesitate to use this term at all within the context of the<br /> Umbra. To provoke religious connotations when dealing<br /> with metaphysical beings of this kind leaves a sour taste in<br /> my mouth, for the Sleepers could easily misinterpret this to<br /> mean &quot;gods&quot; attached to each &quot;religion&quot; for which they<br /> ascribe. However, this category accounts for beings with<br /> such vast influence and power that even the Enlightened<br /> would mistake it for omnipotence. They are of such relative<br /> importance to the Umbra that their sway is, in some ways,<br /> thought to cross all levels, realms and pocket realities.<br /> However, for all the influence held by a divinity, none<br /> of it is direct. It must accomplish all by proxy, through tools<br /> or beings of its own creation. Within all Enlightened knowledge<br /> and experience, a divinity cannot immediately and<br /> irrevocably alter the existence of reality. Certainly it can<br /> command its proxies to do so, but divinities themselves seem<br /> hamstrung by their very existence. Current theories suspect<br /> they may themselves comprise reality, that the very Umbra<br /> is a collection of divinities; that the realm of earth is an<br /> amalgamation of all divinities into a corporeal shell, whereas<br /> other realms are themselves portions of a single divinity. I<br /> grow wary of analogizing the realms beyond earth as the<br /> &quot;internal organs of divinity,&quot; but the theory lends itself to the<br /> true scope of the matter.<br /> <b>For your own context, those amongst your Traditions<br /> refer to these beings as celestines or &quot;uthras.&quot; Within this<br /> redefinition I have wrapped those beings of even greater<br /> power \u2014 &quot;The One,&quot; your &quot;Gaia,&quot; that which your texts<br /> submit as &quot;laldabaoth&quot; and to which humans call &quot;Satan,&quot;<br /> the Umbood known as &quot;the Wyrm,&quot; etc. Functionally there<br /> \u00a9F fllADNESS</b><br /> may be a difference between these beings and celestines, but<br /> these Umbrood are so vast that distinction between them is<br /> rather pointless. To do so is akin to saying &quot;twice infinity&quot; \u2014<br /> pure nonsense. I remain convinced that such a celestial<br /> hierarchy at those levels shall remain ever incomprehensible<br /> to human minds, even Enlightened ones.<br /> As a brief appendix to your comment that Celestines are<br /> themselves influenced by human belief, I hesitate to suggest<br /> that human worship alone remains responsible for the existence<br /> of divinities. Certainly they provide a strong affect<br /> upon these Umbrood. However, to make such an assumption<br /> without any form of direct proof is to accept a belief commonly<br /> held by Sleepers as Truth. To preclude spiritual<br /> arguments, I state that I do not doubt divinities are indeed<br /> affected by Sleeper and Enlightened alike, or that worship is<br /> itself a factor. I simply doubt that worship is solely responsible<br /> for their existence and influence. </div> </div> </div>As for Mage, Incarnas are just avatars of the gods, but not gods themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> AVATAR<br /> <b>More distinct than a divinity, an avatar often encompasses<br /> beings which themselves represent the direct<br /> connection a divinity has to the affectation of reality itself.</b><br /> An avatar is the condensed power of a divinity given form,<br /> focus and direction. It is unknown whether an avatar is a<br /> divine simulacrum &quot;built&quot; and commanded to carry out tasks<br /> (as I would construct automata to carry out more menial<br /> errands), or are perhaps themselves the direct extensions of<br /> divinities who &quot;see through&quot; the avatar's &quot;eyes&quot; and direct its<br /> motions (as I would virtually enter within the Digital Web).<br /> Whatever the truth, the influence of an avatar is much<br /> less than that of a divinity. Whereas divinities themselves<br /> thread themselves throughout the universe, so to speak, an<br /> avatar is limited to the areas in which a divinity bears<br /> influence. Beyond this, avatars are tied to (and in some cases,<br /> represent) specific concepts, often an aspect of the divinity's<br /> influence. Debate still continues whether avatars are themselves<br /> &quot;incarnate,&quot; taking the Umbral analogy of &quot;physical<br /> form,&quot; or whether they are themselves too close to divinity<br /> to ever truly &quot;incorporate.&quot;<br /> Such an idea remains a topic for debate that unfortunately<br /> lies beyond the scope of our text, however interesting<br /> it may be. Regardless, we should mention that there remains<br /> little definitive proof that an avatar has ever directly and<br /> completely entered the realm of earth. Certainly their own<br /> proxies have been known to do so, and perhaps some loose<br /> an aspect of themselves into the realm, but whether they can<br /> actually enter the realm or whether they simply imply they<br /> can remains a point of contention.<br /> <b>Your Tradition calls these beings Incarna or &quot;Aeons,&quot;<br /> an earlier usage. </b>Certain schools of thought believe avatars<br /> are the direct face of worshipped beings. One Enlightened<br /> scholar whom I correspond with suggested to some Sleeper<br /> colleagues that most current human religions venerate the<br /> multiple avatars of a single divinity, in the form of &quot;God&quot; or<br /> &quot;Allah&quot; or &quot;Papa Legba,&quot; amongst others. Unfortunately the<br /> debate ended abruptly when all involved came to blows, so<br /> perhaps we should avoid including </div> </div> </div>Mage Ascension Corebook Revised<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Celestine</b>: A great spirit, essentially a <b>god</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Incarna</b>: Greater spirits; the servants of the Celestines. For<br /> all intents and purposes, <b>demigods</b>. </div> </div> </div><br /> And again, that's true also for Werewolves: Incarna are not gods, Celestines are.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Corebook Revised<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The werewolves hold that the greatest spirit is Gaia.<br /> Below her is the Triat: the Wyld, the Weaver and the Wyrm.<br /> <b>Below the Triat are the Celestines, who are akin to gods</b>.<br /> Below the Celestines are the Incarnae: the lords and kings </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-04-2020, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:09:59-07:00","id":1411900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411887#post1411887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits are Spirits, they are not gods by definition. Even more by Werewolf lore the only thing that can be compared to a god are Celestines, not Incarna.<br /> And in the context of the Wod that's even more true, because we could use mage definitions of goodhood, and we know pretty well that umbrood are not gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some gods are celestines by WW and Mage lore (Jupiter, Luna, Helios...), some others, lesser ones, are Incarnae. Both Celestines and Incarnae are spirits in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:17:41-07:00","id":1411902,"title":"","content":"As stated, Incarnas are not gods, the sources are pretty much clear about it, at most they can be classified as &quot;demigods&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T15:22:51-07:00","id":1411906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411902#post1411902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated, Incarnas are not gods, the sources are pretty much clear about it, at most they can be classified as &quot;demigods&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no issue with that definition but note how Incarnae and Celestines are still spirits.<br /> <br /> Vampires are most definitely NOT spirits, they are spiritually barren.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T02:42:07-07:00","id":1412027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1411851#post1411851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are not gods in any sense of the word. They sometimes manage to create cults that revere them as such but more often hijack existing cults portraying themselves as gods for a subsect of mortals. That is actually the case with Mithras. Check out DA Mage: Grimoire for confirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends on your definition of god. They are, after all, powerful supernatural entities that can grant immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T02:56:58-07:00","id":1412032,"title":"","content":"Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a> said god has a very specific definition in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T05:48:57-07:00","id":1412059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412032#post1412032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12142\" data-vbnamecard=\"12142\">Undead rabbit</a> said god has a very specific definition in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh, Mages use that definition.<br /> <br /> Spirits are just jumped up dream parasites.<br /> <br /> Worshiped by wannabe Klingons like Werewolves. They are unworthy of the title of god, unlike the glory of TZIMISCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T07:56:37-07:00","id":1412087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412059#post1412059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehh, Mages use that definition.<br /> <br /> Spirits are just jumped up dream parasites.<br /> <br /> Worshiped by wannabe Klingons like Werewolves. They are unworthy of the title of god, unlike the glory of TZIMISCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02<br /> <br /> Did you know there was a Byzantine emperor whose surname was Tzimisce?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T08:07:17-07:00","id":1412089,"title":"","content":"Why isn't Baba Yaga more powerful than an Incarna? because Antedeluvians consider it worth playing whole games of faking their death and shit to upgrade to Incarna status. Tzim and Lasombra on are the cusp of Incarna status. Cappy failed at his gambit for it.. and Saulot is still working things out.. of course he also has a step two after &quot;Become yama King&quot; and that's &quot;Become Demon Emperor&quot; <br /> <br /> Conversely Ravana who was a fourth gen may have transcended Baba Yaga by becoming a Yama King.<br /> <br /> Being a Vampire for all their &quot;godly&quot; status limits you. That's why the truly powerful stop being vampires. They become the Abyss. Or Vis or Madness... That's Incarna level power. Baba Yaga... is still recognizably a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T18:35:13-07:00","id":1412197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412089#post1412089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why isn't Baba Yaga more powerful than an Incarna? because Antedeluvians consider it worth playing whole games of faking their death and shit to upgrade to Incarna status. Tzim and Lasombra on are the cusp of Incarna status. Cappy failed at his gambit for it.. and Saulot is still working things out.. of course he also has a step two after &amp;quot;Become yama King&amp;quot; and that's &amp;quot;Become Demon Emperor&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> Conversely Ravana who was a fourth gen may have transcended Baba Yaga by becoming a Yama King.<br /> <br /> Being a Vampire for all their &amp;quot;godly&amp;quot; status limits you. That's why the truly powerful stop being vampires. They become the Abyss. Or Vis or Madness... That's Incarna level power. Baba Yaga... is still recognizably a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T00:07:04-07:00","id":1412228,"title":"","content":"Most of the vampires who claim to be gods are full of BS but some are likely legit. For example, Set is probably just who he claims to be. Keep in mind there is an ancient ghost in the Underworld who claims to be Osiris. And according to him, his brother Set killed him. And that brother Set is the same Set who's a vampire. And he has a son named Horus who came back as a mummy. And Horus claims that that ghost named Osiris is the legit Osiris and that the vampire Set is his uncle and the legit Set. And you have others, such as the god Anubis or the Cult of Isis. It would be pretty easy for Osiris or Horus to say, &quot;That vampire claiming to be Set? He's a fraud, that's not my brother/uncle. He's just stealing the name.&quot; But they both seem to be under the impression that Set is actually their relative of the same name.<br /> <br /> It's possible everyone is lying about their names and relationships with one another and none of them are who they claim to be or related to each other, but at a certain point I just throw up my hands and figure that it's more plausible that this is the same group of people discussed in Egyptian mythology rather than the idea that this group of people are lying and backing one another one another's claims while clawing at each other's throats.<br /> <br /> Of course that's not to say that Set is a &quot;god&quot; god, just that Set was really powerful, people worshiped him like a god, and his relationship with his brother, and nephew and others served as the origin for Egyptian mythology. So he's not an actual deity, but ancient Egypt's myths were about him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T01:10:04-07:00","id":1412233,"title":"","content":"When I'm the storyteller, Set actually IS a god, and the vampires he created (whether through curses, priests petitioning him to raise the dead, etc.) are unrelated but mechanically equivalent to the vampires of other clans. I haven't decided whether all the rest are related and truly descended from Caine, or Lilith, or if there are multiple origins for vampires and the Caine myth is just something that was adopted as an origin story in the last few thousand years. Hell, maybe Tzimisce arrived on a spaceship that crashed in the Antarctic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T01:22:54-07:00","id":1412234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412233#post1412233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I'm the storyteller, Set actually IS a god, and the vampires he created (whether through curses, priests petitioning him to raise the dead, etc.) are unrelated but mechanically equivalent to the vampires of other clans. I haven't decided whether all the rest are related and truly descended from Caine, or Lilith, or if there are multiple origins for vampires and the Caine myth is just something that was adopted as an origin story in the last few thousand years. Hell, maybe Tzimisce arrived on a spaceship that crashed in the Antarctic!</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I take a more Neil Gaiman-esque approach that makes the matter even more bizarre.<br /> <br /> Set is a 3rd generation vampire.<br /> <br /> Osiris is a wraith.<br /> <br /> Horus is a Mummy.<br /> <br /> All three of them inspired a myth and dream so powerful that it created Incarnae in the Umbra of incredible power that were <i>retroactively always in existence and the real gods worshiped by mortals</i>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps even resulting in Set, Horus, and Osiris being named after them.<br /> <br /> It's why Demons from D:TF hate dealing with mages because the mages argue that they can simultaneously predate the universe, be billions of years old, and also the products of the dreams of a small group of Semitic peoples that eventually became very popular.<br /> <br /> Werewolves know it's best to just kill mages for this.<br /> <br /> Changelings, by contrast, would just find the concept self-obvious...which is why no one likes Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-06-2020, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T06:35:56-07:00","id":1412270,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I like your idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T20:32:18-07:00","id":1412377,"title":"","content":"This might be a good time to point out that at least to the Garou, Sutekh is a god. Moreover, he is to the WRITERS of W:tA.<br /> <br /> In the Times of Judgement scenario dealing with the fall of the Silent Striders, he's called a god-vampire and a godling by the text, in what looks to be the &quot;if it's that powerful we might as well call it a god,&quot; approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T20:36:11-07:00","id":1412380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412234#post1412234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, I take a more Neil Gaiman-esque approach that makes the matter even more bizarre.<br /> <br /> Set is a 3rd generation vampire.<br /> <br /> Osiris is a wraith.<br /> <br /> Horus is a Mummy.<br /> <br /> All three of them inspired a myth and dream so powerful that it created Incarnae in the Umbra of incredible power that were <i>retroactively always in existence and the real gods worshiped by mortals</i>.<br /> <br /> Perhaps even resulting in Set, Horus, and Osiris being named after them.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, the first WoD Crossover chronicle in history, and it ended up with all the players hating each other and splitting up to do their own thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T00:51:24-07:00","id":1412402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412380#post1412380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, the first WoD Crossover chronicle in history, and it ended up with all the players hating each other and splitting up to do their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its even funnier if you remember Isis was a Mage and, yes, maybe some of the others were Pooka.<br /> <br /> (More like Egyptian Tuatha De Daanan that are to Pooka what Methuselahs are to Thin Bloods)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1411761-gods-and-vampires?p=1412377#post1412377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a good time to point out that at least to the Garou, Sutekh is a god. Moreover, he is to the WRITERS of W:tA.<br /> <br /> In the Times of Judgement scenario dealing with the fall of the Silent Striders, he's called a god-vampire and a godling by the text, in what looks to be the &quot;if it's that powerful we might as well call it a god,&quot; approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of &quot;Pokemon Fights&quot;, the Garou have defeated manifest Incarnae as well as the Eater of Souls.<br /> <br /> The Silent Striders LOST to Set.<br /> <br /> They also weren't the ones to take down (if taken down she was) Baba Yaga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-07-2020, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-07T07:21:03-07:00","id":1412432,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26275_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26275\" data-vbnamecard=\"26275\">Konigheim Horror</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I totally agree with you guys \ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":